      "headline": "Germany approves new customs powers to seize suspected illicit assets, including cryptoGermany Approves New Customs Powers to Seize Suspected Illicit Assets, Including Crypto Germany’s Bundestag has approved legislation allowing customs authorities to temporarily secure significant assets, including crypto, when there are substantiated doubts about their lawful origin even before a criminal case is opened. The procedure generally targets assets worth more than €100,000, while permanent confiscation would still require a fiscal court ruling. The law is scheduled to take effect on January 1, 2027, subject to Bundesrat approval and formal promulgation. — link",
