      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Chinese Miner Jiang Zhuoer Exits DeFi Altcoins After Market Call Misses, Pauses Trading Jiang Zhuoer, founder of BTC.TOP and a prominent Chinese miner, said he has sold all of his DeFi altcoin holdings and moved to a hedged neutral position after Bitcoin’s latest decline invalidated parts of his earlier bullish thesis. He said BTC broke below support near $63,853 and $64,100 and approached his roughly $61,576 invalidation level, adding that a move below $57,800 in a late-bear-market scenario could bring sharper losses for smaller DeFi tokens. Jiang said he plans to step away from trading for a period before considering new positions. — link",
