    {
      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "64,000 Bitcoin Mining Machines Hijacked, Redirecting 13 EH/s to OCEAN Pool Bitcoin News reported that approximately 64,000 Bitcoin mining machines, representing about 13 EH/s of hashrate, were hijacked around 20:00 U.S. Central Time on November 14. The attackers redirected the hashrate to OCEAN and replaced the mining payout address with one they controlled, briefly pushing the pool's hashrate close to 50 EH/s. CoreX Hosting said the incident appeared to have ended on November 15, with the affected hashrate falling to around 100 PH/s. The attackers failed to mine any blocks and received no block rewards, although affected miners lost mining revenue during the incident. A potential compromise of Luxor Commander software has not been independently confirmed. — link",
